div.p:
Capt. B. C. Creelman, American; First Officer, George N. Armstrong, American;
                    Second Officer, F. Fitzgerald, American; Boatswain, Frank Harris, American;
                    seamen, 
 Fred Phillips, English; J.
                    Lasson and James O’Niel, Americans; Harry Luno, Denmark; John Johnson, Norway;
                    Alexander, Russian; Fred Brown, American; Charles Arthur, German; Harry Hangson,
                    Denmark; Manuel Nelson, Swede; seven Japanese: Ishii Esaku, Matsushinia
                    Torasaburo, Hirahara Rinkichi, Okada Seshiro, Yamamoto Katsuji, Murakami
                    Kurataro, and Horita Hachiro, Cook, Ahau (Bankok, Siam), drowned.
